<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1997 cotton output seen at 1.2 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1997 cotton output seen at 1.2 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's cotton output is seen at 1.2 million 375-lb (170 kg) bales in 1997, the president of Association of Mexican Cotton Growers said Friday.</p>
<p>Salomon Paz said he expected little change from previous years given there had been little movement in surface area under cultivation.</p>
<p>Cotton is grown principally in four northern states, namely Sonora, Coahuila, Chihuahua and Tamaulipas.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
